One common way the Java API is misused is through the improper handling of user input when interacting with the operating system, specifically when using `Runtime.getRuntime().exec()`. This can lead to Command Injection vulnerabilities.

```java
import java.io.*;

public class CommandExecutor {
    public void executeSystemCommand(String filename) {
        try {
            // VULNERABLE: User input is concatenated directly into a shell command.
            // An attacker could provide input like "file.txt; rm -rf /" to execute arbitrary commands.
            String command = "ls -l " + filename;
            Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);

            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println(line);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

